## Summary

This is the **spring-petclinic-rest** Spring Boot app (Maven). The feature area you described lives under the owner-create pipeline (`rest/function/owner/`) and the `util/` package. All four concepts map to real code except **fiscalYear**, which is a *not-yet-implemented* feature described only in a failing/pending acceptance test.

---

## 1. Business-day-adjusted registration date

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/RegistrationDates.java`** — the core logic. Package `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner` (package-private `final class RegistrationDates`).

Key methods:
- `static LocalDate toBusinessDay(LocalDate date)` — rolls a Saturday/Sunday/holiday forward one day at a time until it lands on a business day.
- `static LocalDate effective(LocalDate supplied)` — returns `toBusinessDay(supplied != null ? supplied : LocalDate.now())`.
- `private static boolean isWeekend(LocalDate date)`.
- Holidays are a hardcoded `Set<LocalDate> HOLIDAYS` for 2026: `2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28`.

(Full contents shown earlier — the whole class is the load-bearing logic.)

**Consumers of the business-day adjustment:**
- **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ResolveRegistrationDate.java`** — `public void service(@Val Owner owner)` calls `owner.setRegistrationDate(RegistrationDates.effective(owner.getRegistrationDate()))`. This is the step that stores the adjusted date on the entity.
- **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnsureDailyLimit.java`** — uses `RegistrationDates.effective(...)` to count against the same adjusted day (`DAILY_LIMIT = 100`, throws `DailyLimitExceededException`).
- **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/DailyRegistrations.java`** — `static int countOn(OwnerRepository, LocalDate businessDay)`.
- **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ValidateRegistrationDate.java`** — `public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request)`; rejects future dates with `FutureRegistrationDateException` (does NOT do the business-day roll — only future-date validation).

---

## 2. Membership identifier (with year segment)

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/MembershipNumbers.java`** — package `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.util`, `public final class MembershipNumbers`.

The load-bearing method:
```java
public static String of(Owner owner) {
    if (owner.getCustomerCode() == null || owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {
        return null;
    }
    return String.format("%s-M%02d", owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100);
}
```
Format: `<customerCode>-M<YY>` where `YY` = last two digits of the registration year (e.g. `SYD-SMI-0007-M26`). **This is where the year segment is derived** — `getYear() % 100`. Since it reads `getRegistrationDate()`, it depends on the business-day-adjusted date set by `ResolveRegistrationDate`.

Related: **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/CustomerCode.java`** builds the `<REGION>-<HASH8>` customer-code portion (`of`, `deduplicate`, `regionOf`).

Exposed to the API via **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** — `default String membershipNumber(Owner owner) { return MembershipNumbers.of(owner); }`, mapped to DTO field `membershipNumber`. Also mapped: `checkDigit`, `membershipPoints`, `membershipLevel`.

---

## 3. Tenure (365-day window)

